      "content": "i get the official stance, but that's exactly what they want people to think. if you look at the shift from 432Hz to 440Hz in music and how that correlates with the standardization of the electrical grid, it looks way too intentional to be a coincidence. there's a massive difference in how the nervous system reacts to those two frequencies. can u at least compare the mathematical properties of 432Hz vs 440Hz and explain why the 440Hz standard is often criticized by researchers for being 'unnatural' or dissonant?",
